ther Dunlap's recent polling edge is real or a Democratic-sponsor artifact.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Jared Golden (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Maine's 2nd District is an open seat after Democrat Jared Golden's retirement, in a district that leans Republican by about four points. Former Governor Paul LePage faces State Auditor Matt Dunlap. LePage holds a large financial advantage, with roughly $1.7 million on hand to Dunlap's $229,000, though outside spending has so far been minimal on both sides.\n\nExpert ratings split between Lean/Likely Republican and Tossup, and prediction markets tilt Republican. Yet the most recent polls, including a neutral University of New Hampshire survey, show Dunlap slightly ahead, and LePage has worked to distance himself from Trump on some issues in their debates. The race sits on a knife's edge with a modest Republican tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4353, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4338, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4042, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4713, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3776, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3456, "margin": -2.0}]}